      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Left ventricular diastolic filling measurements were determined by means of standard consecutive R-wave gating, list mode acquisition, and alternate R-wave gating. Time-activity curves obtained by the latter two methods were equally accurate in quantifying rapid, slow, and atrial left ventricular filling, whereas curves obtained by means of standard gating were inadequate for this purpose."},
